{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 41, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan!\n\nJust back from an incredible trip to Japan, and I'm already dreaming of going back! It was a whirlwind of ancient traditions and futuristic technology – a truly captivating contrast.\n\nMy journey started in Tokyo, a sensory overload in the best way. Shibuya Crossing was exhilarating, and exploring the quirky shops of Harajuku was a highlight. I spent hours wandering through serene gardens, finding pockets of tranquility amidst the bustling city.\n\nNext, I took the Shinkansen (bullet train!) to Kyoto, the cultural heart of Japan. Temples and shrines were everywhere, each more beautiful than the last. I loved strolling through Gion, hoping to catch a glimpse of a geisha. The Fushimi Inari Shrine, with its thousands of vibrant red torii gates, was breathtaking.\n\nFood was, of course, a major focus! From delicious ramen and sushi to delicate wagashi (Japanese sweets), every meal was a treat. I even braved a traditional tea ceremony – a wonderfully calming experience.\n\nNavigating the language barrier was a challenge, but everyone was so incredibly helpful and kind. I learned a few basic phrases, which definitely came in handy.\n\nJapan exceeded all my expectations. It's a country that truly nourishes the soul. If you're looking for an adventure, I highly recommend adding Japan to your travel list!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0011177966371178627}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.18502815067768097}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0015026956098154187}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.1426810771226883}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.11408442258834839}, {"token": "!", "logprob": -1.5096462965011597}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -4.529942543740617e-06}, {"token